    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d913">

                <pb facs="0863" n="857" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg857"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">390D.11/184: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-21T17:00:00+02:00">November 21, 1939—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:02 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>147. Your telegram No. 53, November 20, 6 p.m.<anchor n="13" xml:id="d913-f1"/>
                    The Foreign Office has informally submitted to us a counterproposal which
                    however is quite at variance with our ideas in a number of points and requires
                    considerable discussion before we can contemplate its taking a form that we
                    could submit for your approval.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
